course: dictionary
lesson: 4038
title: Context clues: gecko
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: You may meet a new word like gecko and not know it. Context clues help. Read the words around it: a small lizard, warm countries, climbing walls. These clues tell you what kind of creature it is.
explain: «Geckos stick to glass with millions of tiny toe hairs» tells you a gecko can climb smooth glass. Use the clues to make a guess, then check it by putting your meaning back into the sentence.
explain: Science texts may use harder words like molecules and forces. You do not need to know them all. Skip them, read on, and come back later, or check a dictionary.
fact: A gecko is a small lizard that lives in warm countries.
fact: Geckos have sticky toe pads, with tiny hairs, that let them climb walls and walk on ceilings.
fact: Some geckos can drop their tails to escape danger.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, geckos live in gardens and houses, and some are kept as pets.
fact: Gecko is a noun, and its plural can be geckos or geckoes.
exercise: «Geckos stick to glass with millions of tiny toe hairs.» What is a gecko? | A tall tree in a dry forest | *A small lizard that lives in warm countries | A type of glass | A kind of fish that swims in cold seas
exercise: «Some geckos can drop their tails to escape.» What does escape mean? | To catch a fly for dinner | To climb a tall tree | *To get away from danger | To fall asleep in the sun
exercise: Where do geckos live in Australia and New Zealand? | Under the sea | Only on high snowy mountains | Inside volcanoes | *In gardens and houses
test: Lily reads «Geckos use their feet to grip.» What helps geckos grip? | A thick coat of fur | Long wings on their backs | Sharp teeth in their mouths | *Tiny hairs on their feet
test: Which phrase names the sticky feet of a gecko? | warm countries | *gecko feet | leopard gecko | ceilings
exam: Jayden says «gecko» must be a bird because it sounds like a chirp. What is the best clue to check? | It is a fish that swims in the sea | *The text says a gecko is a small lizard | It must be a bird because of the sound | It is a plant that grows in gardens
